From: sheng-development
Subject: [PATCH] Allocate the client tables before find_sensors() can bail

pmaports' "WIP: Do not exit based on sensor events" drops the
g_main_loop_quit() from the bail path of name_acquired_handler() so the
daemon survives having no sensors and waits for hotplug. But bail is taken
before the loop that allocates data->clients[], so the daemon then serves
D-Bus with every client hash table still NULL:

  g_hash_table_insert_internal: assertion 'hash_table != NULL' failed
  ERROR:../src/iio-sensor-proxy.c:452:client_vanished_cb: assertion failed: (ht)

client_vanished_cb aborts on the first watched name that disappears, which
on sheng is every boot. The same bail also skipped the "uevent" signal
connection, so the hotplug the WIP patch exists to wait for never arrived
either.

Allocate the tables and connect the handler before find_sensors() runs.
---
 src/iio-sensor-proxy.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -750,18 +750,21 @@
 	guint i;

 	data->client = g_udev_client_new (subsystems);
-	if (!find_sensors (data->client, data))
-		goto bail;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_SENSOR_TYPES; i++) {
+		data->clients[i] = create_clients_hash_table ();
+		data->sensor_startup_dbus_invocations_delayed[i] = g_ptr_array_new ();
+	}

 	g_signal_connect (G_OBJECT (data->client), "uevent",
 			  G_CALLBACK (sensor_changes), data);

+	if (!find_sensors (data->client, data))
+		goto bail;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < NUM_SENSOR_TYPES; i++) {
 		SensorDevice *sensor_device;

-		data->clients[i] = create_clients_hash_table ();
-		data->sensor_startup_dbus_invocations_delayed[i] = g_ptr_array_new ();
-
 		if (!driver_type_exists (data, i))
 			continue;

